{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00297",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.55,
      "end_seconds": 2.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Hi there, come on in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 2.59,
      "end_seconds": 5.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Thanks, doctor. It's been a long few days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 7.4,
      "end_seconds": 11.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.2,
      "end_seconds": 17.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Please do. Extra information is always welcome. What seems to be the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.66,
      "end_seconds": 24.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.12,
      "text": "Yeah, um, it's tightness in my chest when I walk. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.97,
      "end_seconds": 30.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "When did you first notice it? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.71,
      "end_seconds": 35.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "It's been going on for about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.56,
      "end_seconds": 39.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "And what do you do to cope with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.14,
      "end_seconds": 43.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "It settles a little with stopping to rest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.84,
      "end_seconds": 47.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "How would you describe it, mild, moderate, severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.6,
      "end_seconds": 51.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Pretty severe, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.67,
      "end_seconds": 55.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Is it constant, or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.66,
      "end_seconds": 58.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "It happens on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.61,
      "end_seconds": 62.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.86,
      "end_seconds": 67.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Breathlessness on exertion goes along with it, most of the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.36,
      "end_seconds": 73.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 73.62,
      "end_seconds": 77.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.2,
      "end_seconds": 89.58,
      "duration_seconds": 11.38,
      "text": "I was getting to that! As for breathlessness on exertion, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.1,
      "end_seconds": 93.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.08,
      "end_seconds": 98.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Resting helps a bit. I'd say severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.04,
      "end_seconds": 100.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Right, what about cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.93,
      "end_seconds": 103.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Not at all, no cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 104.36,
      "end_seconds": 108.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "So, actually, doctor, I did notice cough. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.39,
      "end_seconds": 114.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.05,
      "end_seconds": 123.67,
      "duration_seconds": 8.62,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Let me check a few things. Any pain at rest or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.35,
      "end_seconds": 133.17,
      "duration_seconds": 8.82,
      "text": "No, no pain at rest, no fever. I was sweating with it at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.26,
      "end_seconds": 137.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Any swelling in the ankles, fainting or palpitations at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.33,
      "end_seconds": 141.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "No, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.41,
      "end_seconds": 145.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.19,
      "end_seconds": 147.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.29,
      "end_seconds": 151.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.78,
      "end_seconds": 160.05,
      "duration_seconds": 7.27,
      "text": "I've got diabetes. I've had high blood pressure for nearly five years now. I've had high cholesterol, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.67,
      "end_seconds": 166.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.97,
      "text": "Okay, high cholesterol, that's already on your record. Good to know. Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.31,
      "end_seconds": 173.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.03,
      "text": "Yes, shellfish, it gives me vomiting. Uh, yes, I'm allergic to latex."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.57,
      "end_seconds": 176.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.44,
      "end_seconds": 181.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 182.45,
      "end_seconds": 189.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.82,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the glimepiride was 4 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.63,
      "end_seconds": 193.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Hm, that's different. Is the latest prescription anywhere near you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.96,
      "end_seconds": 203.53,
      "duration_seconds": 9.57,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. I'm on ramipril, 5 milligrams, every morning for my blood pressure. Rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.98,
      "end_seconds": 206.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.47,
      "end_seconds": 211.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Nearly five years now. Aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.82,
      "end_seconds": 214.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "So, have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.5,
      "end_seconds": 217.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.36,
      "end_seconds": 224.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.54,
      "end_seconds": 231.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "My father was diabetic. My mother has diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.19,
      "end_seconds": 235.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.72,
      "end_seconds": 250.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Just relax your arm..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.78,
      "end_seconds": 265.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 151 over 100, pulse 91. And saturation 97 percent, temperature 36.4."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.79,
      "end_seconds": 267.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.66,
      "end_seconds": 271.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.22,
      "end_seconds": 276.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.95,
      "end_seconds": 278.65,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.79,
      "end_seconds": 281.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Take a breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.57,
      "end_seconds": 293.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Lungs are clear and there's no swelling in your ankles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.24,
      "end_seconds": 295.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Let me press here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.13,
      "end_seconds": 310.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal, no murmurs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.16,
      "end_seconds": 334.65,
      "duration_seconds": 18.49,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Okay, so my impression is this: My working impression is angina-type chest pain. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I can't rule out gastro-oesophageal reflux yet. A musculoskeletal cause is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 336.92,
      "end_seconds": 338.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Is it something serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.23,
      "end_seconds": 362.61,
      "duration_seconds": 23.38,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like angina-type chest pain, but I'd like to confirm. Let's get an ECG, for chest tightness. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Let's get an echocardiogram, for chest tightness. Let's use GTN spray, 0.4 milligrams, when the chest tightness comes, as needed. That should help with chest tightness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.56,
      "end_seconds": 385.87,
      "duration_seconds": 22.31,
      "text": "Don't push through the chest tightness, stop, sit down, and use the spray if I've given it to you. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 387.02,
      "end_seconds": 388.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.71,
      "end_seconds": 397.67,
      "duration_seconds": 8.96,
      "text": "Please don't sit on it if the chest tightness comes at rest or lasts more than fifteen minutes. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 398.74,
      "end_seconds": 400.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.01,
      "end_seconds": 406.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "Please come and see me after the results are back. Alright, that's everything from me. Any other questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 408.04,
      "end_seconds": 409.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "No questions. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 409.97,
      "end_seconds": 411.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}